title: Introduce the pallet unpaid-transact for Polkadot
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Add the pallet `unpaid_transact` in `polkadot-runtime-parachains`, and its XCM barrier
    `AllowUnpaidTransact`.

    They let a non-system parachain have a few calls dispatched as itself without payment. The
    barrier lets through a message made of `UnpaidExecution` and one `Transact` with
    `OriginKind::Native`, for a call in `AllowedCalls`, if the message weighs at most
    `MaxWeight`, and `MaxPerWindow` times per `Window` blocks for each parachain. The barrier does
    not decode the call: `AllowedCalls` is a `ContainsCallVariant` that is asked for the pallet
    index and the call index, which are the first two bytes of the encoded call. Only the messages
    that the barrier lets through are counted.

    What the pallet holds for a parachain that is offboarded is removed, once the window of the
    parachain is over, by the call `remove_offboarded`, which anybody can submit without a
    signature, and which the offchain worker submits every `CleanupPeriod` blocks.

    Westend has the pallet and the barrier, with no allowed call yet.

    Add the trait `ContainsCallVariant` in `frame-support`: a set of call variants of the runtime,
    each identified by its pallet index and its call index, whatever the arguments of the call. It
    is implemented for tuples, `Everything` and `Nothing`.
crates:
- name: frame-support
  bump: minor
- name: polkadot-runtime-parachains
  bump: minor
- name: westend-runtime
  bump: major
